# PWA shell layout — DO NOT BREAK without explicit user approval

This app has a **verified iPhone PWA layout** (pinned frosted bottom nav + scrollable content). The user has marked it as perfect. Treat these files and patterns as protected.

## Before editing protected layout code

1. **STOP** and tell the user which file/pattern you are about to change and **what will break** (scroll, nav gap, blur, header behavior).
2. **Do not proceed** unless the user explicitly confirms they accept the risk, or the change is clearly cosmetic (colors, copy, icons) with zero layout/class/structure impact.
3. After any approved layout change, run `npm run check:shell` and verify on iPhone PWA if possible.

## Protected files (highest risk)

| File | Why |
|------|-----|
| `src/app/globals.css` | `100vh` standalone body, `.app-shell`, `.page-scroll`, `.bottom-nav`, `--bottom-nav-offset` |
| `src/app/layout.tsx` | `overflow-hidden` on html/body, `viewportFit: cover`, standalone inline script |
| `src/components/AppShell.tsx` | Flex shell; `overflow-hidden` + `min-h-0` chain |
| `src/components/BottomNav.tsx` | Must stay `absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0` for frosted blur over scrolling content |
| `src/components/StandaloneClass.tsx` | Sets `data-standalone` for iOS PWA CSS |
| `src/components/BrowseFeed.tsx` | Home feed scroll + compact shelf overlay (different but equally fragile) |

## Canonical page pattern (Kart, Piles, Profile, Toy detail)

Shelf-header pages **must** use this structure:

```tsx
<AppShell>
  <div className="flex min-h-0 flex-1 flex-col overflow-hidden">
    <ShelfHeader ... />
    <div className="page-scroll star-field min-h-0 flex-1 ... scroll-pad-bottom">
      {/* scrollable content */}
    </div>
  </div>
</AppShell>
```

Required classes on the scroll region: `page-scroll`, `min-h-0`, `flex-1`, `scroll-pad-bottom`.

## Home / Browse feed (different pattern — also protected)

- Outer: `relative flex min-h-0 flex-1 flex-col` (no `overflow-hidden` on outer — shelf overlay needs it)
- Scroller: `page-scroll star-field min-h-0 flex-1`
- Bottom padding: `scroll-pad-bottom` on the feed grid, not the scroller root
- Do not pin the expanded header/filters; they scroll with the feed

## iPhone PWA rules (do not revert)

- **Standalone body height: `100vh`**, not `100dvh` — WebKit PWA bug leaves ~34px gap below nav with `100dvh`
- **Never** `calc(100dvh + env(safe-area-inset-bottom))` on body/shell — double-counts safe area
- Bottom nav: absolute overlay + `padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom)` in CSS
- Body/html: `overflow: hidden`; only `.page-scroll` regions scroll

## Safe changes (no warning needed)

Copy, colors, toy data, icons, filter logic, kart store — anything that does not touch flex/overflow/height/positioning/safe-area/viewport.

## Validation

Run `npm run check:shell` before finishing any task that touches layout files. Fix failures or revert.
